    {
      "type": "object",
      "entries": [
        [
          "formattedValue",
          "17 November 2026 update: Full original theorem passed root manuscript, proof, supporting-material and primary-source review, alongside independent scope and adversarial reviews. All 25 geometric fifth-kernel points (including the origin) are covered on the fixed regular-pentagon model's smooth normalization throughout the stated characteristic-zero range, including the allowed plane cusp. Exact division-field degree/group claims are over K=Q(sqrt5), with the generic K(lambda) statement separate. The contribution is credited as an explicit bridge to established Tate-family results; no exclusive-priority claim, external human peer review or formal certification. Native record version 1.0 and original files remain unchanged. Preparing the private research article; canonical remains blank pending live publication and display checks. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/bbfb7abf5c56e3f8d090e125784ff357138076fb/research_website_catalogue_20261024/papers/23137834/reviews/root-continuation-20261117/ROOT_REVIEW.md\n\nEarlier review and inventory notes:\n16 November 2026 update: Substantive review has begun. Two independent scope and adversarial families personally read the complete published manuscript and fresh PDF pages and sealed their own source-first INITIAL derivations before supporting programs, archived opinions and outside proofs. Both families have frozen complete review packets. Root's own source-first assessment and full original-claim disposition remain pending; no scientific pass or public page is approved. Native originals are checksum-bound and unchanged. The version/date here are native metadata; no root claim of a printed numeric version. Canonical remains blank. Evidence: https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/774169ab882ba1de6268868d1cbadc3a43ef44ff/research_website_catalogue_20261024/papers/23137834/reviews/scope-sol/FINAL.json\n\nEarlier inventory note:\nPublished paper record with checksum-bound manuscript; deep review still required."
